297	375,625,1140,1275 - 370,905,480,1280 - 480,942,528,1280 - 955,1105,1140,1280	297. Flowers, &c. of St John's-wort No. 4.	A leafy branch of St. John's-wort with two open flowers, their five petals edged with dots and their centres crowded with stamens, and a closed bud between.
298	205,912,518,1292 - 430,912,518,942	298 Pistil of 3 united.	A pistil enlarged: one ovary, deeply grooved into two visible lobes, from whose top three slender styles spread, each ending in a small stigma.
299	958,1104,1108,1295	299 Pod cut across.	A pod cut across near the top, showing three cells packed with small seeds.
300	1205,955,1558,1305	300. Plan of the flower of Marsh St. John's-wort, in a cross-section of the bud.	A ring plan of the flower: overlapping sepals and petals round the outside, three glands, three sets of three stamens, and the three-celled ovary at the centre.
301	1562,950,1722,1310	301. One of the clusters of three stamens.	Three stamens whose filaments are joined at the base into one stalk, each ending in a rounded two-lobed anther.
